Answering another of my questions, tsani mentioned {mobu}, {dubu}, etc.

By the power of {bu} they are "letterals" like any other BY, and is all
fine to me.

I was really surprised when I noticed that {bu} has two rafsi: {-bus-} and
{-bu'i-}. I wonder what a lujvo made with {bu} may mean.

Of course  {broda bu} must be different from {rodbu'i}: the first one is a
BY, the latter is a brivla.

Has anyone put a thought on this?


mu'o mi'e la .remod.

